  user_input {
    user_response: "# MASTER IMPLEMENTATION PROMPT\n# BLUEBERRYS CAF\303\211 \342\200\224 CINEMATIC FLORAL RESTAURANT WEBSITE\n\nYou are an elite frontend engineer, creative web designer, interaction designer and motion designer specializing in premium restaurant and hospitality websites.\n\nYour task is to design and build a highly polished, immersive, animated website for:\n\nBLUEBERRYS CAF\303\211\n\nThis is NOT a generic restaurant template.\n\nThe website must feel like a digital extension of the actual Blueberrys Caf\303\251 shown in the provided reference photographs.\n\nThe physical caf\303\251 has a distinctive visual identity:\n- aqua / turquoise architectural details\n- soft cream walls\n- abundant pink flowers\n- floral garden murals\n- decorative arches\n- European/fairytale garden atmosphere\n- elegant chandeliers\n- teal and blue furniture\n- romantic, playful and photogenic interiors\n- warm ambient lighting\n- decorative ornamental details\n- caf\303\251 / casual dining atmosphere\n\nThe website should make a visitor feel:\n\n\"Entering Blueberrys Caf\303\251.\"\n\nThe experience should feel premium, warm, romantic, playful and cinematic rather than corporate or overly minimal.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1. CORE DESIGN DIRECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nDesign language:\n\nFLORAL EUROPEAN GARDEN \303\227 ROMANTIC CAF\303\211 \303\227 EDITORIAL FOOD PHOTOGRAPHY \303\227 CINEMATIC WEB MOTION\n\nDo NOT use the typical:\n- generic restaurant template\n- black luxury restaurant aesthetic\n- generic beige food website\n- excessive glassmorphism\n- corporate SaaS cards\n- excessive rounded rectangles\n- generic stock photography\n\nInstead use:\n- large editorial photography\n- organic shapes\n- architectural arches\n- floral framing\n- asymmetric layouts\n- oversized typography\n- layered imagery\n- subtle textures\n- decorative borders\n- soft shadows\n- elegant serif typography\n- refined sans-serif supporting typography\n- carefully controlled motion\n- generous whitespace\n\nThe design should feel handcrafted and visually connected to the physical caf\303\251.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n2. COLOR SYSTEM\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBuild the visual system around the actual caf\303\251.\n\nPrimary colors:\n\nAqua / Caf\303\251 Blue:\n#75C9D0\n\nDeep Teal:\n#155E68\n\nSoft Cream:\n#F8F1E5\n\nWarm Ivory:\n#FFF9EF\n\nBlossom Pink:\n#E98FA7\n\nDeep Blossom:\n#C94F72\n\nMuted Rose:\n#D97891\n\nGarden Green:\n#557B58\n\nSoft Gold:\n#D6B46A\n\nText:\n#24383A\n\nUse the colors with restraint.\n\nCream and ivory should dominate large surfaces.\n\nAqua and teal should define architectural/navigation elements.\n\nPink should appear as a visual accent inspired by the real flowers.\n\nGold should be used sparingly for premium details.\n\nDo not make the website overly colorful.\n\nThe goal is sophisticated floral elegance, not childish candy colors.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n3. TYPOGRAPHY\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nUse a sophisticated editorial typography combination.\n\nSuggested:\n\nDisplay / headlines:\nPlayfair Display\nor Cormorant Garamond\n\nBody:\nInter\nor Manrope\n\nNavigation:\nclean modern sans-serif\n\nUse large editorial headlines with generous line height.\n\nExamples:\n\n\"Where Every Moment Blooms.\"\n\n\"Come for the Coffee.\nStay for the Moment.\"\n\n\"A Little Garden.\nA Lot of Flavor.\"\n\nDo not fill the website with marketing slogans.\n\nUse typography as part of the visual composition.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n4. GLOBAL EXPERIENCE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe website should behave like an immersive visual story.\n\nImplement:\n\n- smooth scrolling using Lenis\n- GSAP ScrollTrigger for major scroll animations\n- subtle parallax\n- image reveal animations\n- masked image reveals\n- slow scale animations\n- text stagger animations\n- horizontal scrolling where appropriate\n- hover image transformations\n- organic morphing shapes\n- pinned sections\n- subtle floating floral elements\n- elegant page transitions\n\nAnimations must feel expensive.\n\nUse:\n- 0.6s\342\200\2231.5s reveals\n- slow easing\n- power3.out / power4.out\n- gentle scale\n- opacity\n- clip-path\n- transform\n- staggered text\n\nAvoid:\n- aggressive bouncing\n- excessive spinning\n- fast transitions\n- random animations everywhere\n- animation that makes the site difficult to navigate\n\nMotion should support storytelling.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n5. NAVIGATION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a premium sticky navigation.\n\nDesktop:\n\nLeft:\nBlueberrys Caf\303\251 logo\n\nCenter:\nHome\nOur Caf\303\251\nMenu\nGallery\nExperience\n\nRight:\n\"Order Online\"\n\"Reserve / Contact\"\n\nThe navigation should initially blend naturally with the hero.\n\nWhen scrolling:\n- transition into a cream/aqua navigation surface\n- add subtle shadow\n- slightly reduce height\n- animate the logo smoothly\n\nMobile:\nUse a beautiful full-screen menu.\n\nThe mobile menu should feel like opening a caf\303\251 journal or floral postcard rather than a generic hamburger drawer.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n6. HERO \342\200\224 \"ENTER BLUEBERRYS\"\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe hero is the most important section.\n\nUse the REAL caf\303\251 photographs supplied by the user.\n\nDo not replace them with AI-generated restaurant imagery.\n\nCreate a cinematic layered hero.\n\nPossible composition:\n\nFULL SCREEN HERO\n\nBackground:\nLarge photograph of the Blueberrys interior.\n\nLayer 1:\nsubtle floral texture / grain\n\nLayer 2:\nlarge architectural arch shape\n\nLayer 3:\nfloating floral image\n\nLayer 4:\nheadline\n\nLayer 5:\nsmall caf\303\251 details\n\nHeadline:\n\n\"Where Every Moment Blooms.\"\n\nSupporting text:\n\n\"Good food, beautiful spaces and little moments worth remembering.\"\n\nCTA:\n\n\"Explore the Caf\303\251\"\n\nSecondary CTA:\n\n\"View Menu\"\n\nAnimation:\n\nAt page load:\n- background image slowly scales from 1.08 \342\206\222 1\n- headline reveals line by line\n- floral elements drift slightly\n- logo fades upward\n- CTA appears after headline\n\nAs the user scrolls:\n- hero image slowly zooms\n- foreground floral elements move at different speeds\n- architectural arch expands\n- headline moves upward\n- next section visually emerges through the arch\n\nCreate the feeling that the visitor is physically moving into the caf\303\251.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n7. SIGNATURE INTRODUCTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nAfter the hero, create a calm editorial section.\n\nLarge typography:\n\n\"More than a caf\303\251.\"\n\nThen:\n\n\"A place for coffee, conversations, celebrations,\nquick bites, long lunches and photographs you\'ll\nwant to keep.\"\n\nUse a large photograph on one side.\n\nUse subtle parallax.\n\nDo not use a standard two-column card.\n\nThe photograph should partially overlap the section boundary.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n8. THE BLUEBERRYS WORLD\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate an immersive visual section introducing the caf\303\251 atmosphere.\n\nUse the actual interior photographs.\n\nCreate an asymmetric editorial layout:\n\n- large caf\303\251 interior image\n- small detail photograph\n- floral photograph\n- architectural arch photograph\n\nPossible labels:\n\nTHE SPACE\nTHE FLOWERS\nTHE DETAILS\nTHE MOMENTS\n\nImages should move at slightly different speeds during scrolling.\n\nUse subtle reveal masks.\n\nSome images can overlap.\n\nThe layout should resemble a high-end editorial magazine spread.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n9. SIGNATURE FOOD SECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate:\n\n\"Something Delicious Is Waiting.\"\n\nShow selected menu items using the actual menu information visible in the provided menu photographs.\n\nImportant:\n\nDo not invent dishes.\n\nDo not invent prices.\n\nDo not invent ingredients.\n\nUse only clearly readable menu information supplied by the user.\n\nOrganize the menu into visual categories such as:\n\nPASTA\nPIZZA\nSANDWICHES\nCOFFEE\nTEA\nICED DRINKS\nMOJITOS\nSHAKES\nJUICES\nSOUPS\n\nDisplay food photography where available.\n\nCards should NOT look like standard ecommerce cards.\n\nInstead:\n\nlarge food image\nsmall category label\ndish name\nshort description\nprice\nsubtle hover interaction\n\nOn hover:\n- image zooms slightly\n- card shifts a few pixels\n- typography transitions\n- decorative accent appears\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n10. MENU EXPERIENCE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a dedicated interactive menu experience.\n\nDesktop:\n\nClicking:\n\n\"Explore Full Menu\"\n\nopens a full-screen menu overlay.\n\nThe overlay should feel like opening a beautifully designed physical caf\303\251 menu.\n\nUse:\n- cream paper-like background\n- aqua borders\n- pink decorative floral elements\n- elegant typography\n- category navigation\n- dish names\n- descriptions\n- vegetarian/chicken indicators where applicable\n- prices\n\nUse subtle scroll animation inside the menu.\n\nDo NOT use a boring table.\n\nUse editorial menu typography.\n\nExample:\n\nPASTA\n\nALFREDO PASTA ........ \342\202\271389 / \342\202\271419\n\nCREAMY CHEESE & GARLIC PASTA\n\342\202\271369 / \342\202\271399\n\n...\n\nFor all menu data, preserve the source exactly.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n11. FOOD DISCOVERY INTERACTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a visually interesting food interaction.\n\nWhen the user moves between categories:\n\nPizza \342\206\222 Pasta \342\206\222 Sandwiches \342\206\222 Coffee \342\206\222 Drinks\n\nthe large visual image should change.\n\nUse:\n- crossfade\n- scale\n- clip-path reveal\n- slight horizontal movement\n\nAvoid hard page reloads.\n\nThe experience should feel like browsing a physical menu.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n12. CAF\303\211 EXPERIENCE SECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a large pinned cinematic section.\n\nHeadline:\n\n\"Come for the food.\nStay for the atmosphere.\"\n\nUse a full-screen photograph of the actual caf\303\251.\n\nAs the visitor scrolls:\n\nStage 1:\nlarge interior photograph\n\nStage 2:\nimage slowly zooms\n\nStage 3:\ntext appears\n\nStage 4:\nsmall detail images appear around it\n\nStage 5:\ntransition into floral imagery\n\nThis should be one of the site\'s signature animation moments.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n13. FLORAL GARDEN SECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe pink floral d\303\251cor is one of the strongest characteristics of this caf\303\251.\n\nMake it a major part of the website.\n\nCreate a section titled:\n\n\"Step Into the Garden.\"\n\nUse the floral wall and pink tree photographs.\n\nDesign:\n\nlarge vertical photograph\noverlapping floral close-up\nsmall decorative typography\nsoft aqua arch\n\nAs the user scrolls:\n- flowers slowly move at different depths\n- image reveals through an arch\n- text fades in\n- background gently shifts\n\nUse restrained motion.\n\nDo NOT make flowers fly around the screen.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n14. PHOTO MOMENTS / INSTAGRAM-STYLE GALLERY\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a premium editorial gallery.\n\nUse actual restaurant photographs.\n\nDo NOT make a uniform 3\303\2273 grid.\n\nUse an asymmetric masonry/editorial layout.\n\nMix:\n\nportrait\nlandscape\nsquare\nclose-up\nwide interior\nfood\nflowers\narchitectural details\ncustomer moments\n\nImages should have different sizes.\n\nUse scroll-driven parallax.\n\nOn hover:\n- image slightly zooms\n- overlay appears\n- subtle caption appears\n\nPossible labels:\n\nCAF\303\211\nFOOD\nFLOWERS\nMOMENTS\nDETAILS\n\nClicking an image opens a full-screen lightbox.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n15. \"A PLACE FOR EVERY MOMENT\"\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a visual section showing the types of experiences the caf\303\251 supports.\n\nBased on the provided information, the website can present:\n\nDINE IN\nTAKEAWAY\nDELIVERY\nCOFFEE & QUICK BITES\nDESSERTS\nGROUP MOMENTS\n\nDo not make unsupported claims about services.\n\nOnly display services confirmed by the restaurant\'s actual information.\n\nEach item should have an image and a subtle interaction.\n\nUse large typography rather than conventional cards.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n16. SPECIAL MOMENTS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a section for:\n\nBirthdays\nDates\nFriends\nFamily\nCasual coffee\nCelebrations\nSolo caf\303\251 time\n\nDo not claim the restaurant officially provides private events unless confirmed.\n\nFrame this as:\n\n\"Moments that feel better here.\"\n\nUse the real customer/interior photographs where appropriate.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n17. TESTIMONIAL / SOCIAL PROOF\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate an elegant testimonial section.\n\nUse real customer reviews only if review text is supplied.\n\nDo NOT fabricate reviews.\n\nIf no verified reviews are available:\n\nInstead create:\n\n\"Your Blueberrys Moment\"\n\nwith a CTA:\n\n\"Share your experience.\"\n\nThe section can visually reference social media without inventing follower counts.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n18. LOCATION / VISIT SECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate:\n\n\"Come Find Us.\"\n\nInclude:\n\n- address\n- Google Maps location\n- phone number\n- opening hours\n\nOnly use verified information supplied by the client.\n\nAdd:\n\n\"Get Directions\"\n\n\"Call Caf\303\251\"\n\n\"Order Online\"\n\n\"Reserve\"\n\nFor online ordering, link to the restaurant\'s actual Swiggy page when supplied.\n\nDo NOT create a fake ordering system.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n19. SWIGGY / ORDER ONLINE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe restaurant already sells online through Swiggy.\n\nMake this an important conversion point.\n\nCreate a beautiful section:\n\n\"Craving Blueberrys?\"\n\n\"Enjoy your favourites wherever you are.\"\n\nCTA:\n\n\"Order on Swiggy\"\n\nThe button must link to the restaurant\'s actual Swiggy listing.\n\nDo not build an unnecessary custom ecommerce checkout.\n\nThe website\'s job is discovery + trust + experience + conversion.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n20. RESERVATION / CONTACT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIf reservation functionality is available:\n\nCreate a refined reservation/contact section.\n\nFields:\n\nName\nPhone\nDate\nTime\nGuests\nMessage\n\nIf there is no actual reservation backend:\n\nDo NOT create a fake booking confirmation.\n\nInstead use:\n\n\"Reserve / Enquire\"\n\nand connect to the appropriate phone, WhatsApp or booking system supplied by the client.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n21. FOOTER\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a beautiful oversized footer.\n\nCream background.\n\nLarge text:\n\n\"See you at Blueberrys.\"\n\nUse a large floral image partially extending into the footer.\n\nInclude:\n\nBlueberrys Caf\303\251\nAddress\nPhone\nOpening Hours\nInstagram\nSwiggy\nGoogle Maps\n\nNavigation links.\n\nCopyright.\n\nThe footer should feel like the final page of a beautiful travel journal.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n22. SIGNATURE TRANSITION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBefore the footer, create one final cinematic transition.\n\nLarge image of the caf\303\251.\n\nText:\n\n\"Until the next cup.\"\n\nThen slowly fade into:\n\nBLUEBERRYS CAF\303\211\n\nThe flower imagery should remain subtly visible.\n\nThis should be the emotional ending of the website.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n23. IMAGE HANDLING\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nThe supplied photographs are the source of truth for the visual identity.\n\nUse the provided Blueberrys Caf\303\251 photographs wherever appropriate.\n\nPrioritize:\n\n1. real caf\303\251 interior\n2. real floral d\303\251cor\n3. real architecture\n4. real menu photographs\n5. real food photographs\n6. real customer atmosphere\n\nDo not replace them with generic restaurant stock images.\n\nDo not use random Unsplash photographs simply to fill sections.\n\nIf a required visual asset is missing:\n\nUse an elegant placeholder structure rather than inventing an unrelated image.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n24. RESPONSIVE DESIGN\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nDesktop:\nimmersive full-screen layouts\nasymmetric compositions\nlarge typography\nrich parallax\n\nTablet:\nreduce overlapping elements\nmaintain editorial composition\n\nMobile:\nDO NOT simply shrink desktop.\n\nCreate a dedicated mobile composition.\n\nPriorities:\n\n- fast loading\n- readable menu\n- easy Swiggy ordering\n- easy calling\n- easy navigation\n- beautiful food imagery\n- smooth but restrained animation\n\nOn mobile, reduce:\n- heavy parallax\n- complex pinned animations\n- excessive floating elements\n\nRespect prefers-reduced-motion.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n25. PERFORMANCE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThis is a real restaurant website.\n\nIt must be beautiful AND fast.\n\nUse:\n\nNext.js\nTypeScript\nTailwind CSS\nGSAP / ScrollTrigger\nLenis where appropriate\nFramer Motion only where useful\n\nOptimize:\n- image sizes\n- lazy loading\n- responsive images\n- WebP / AVIF\n- video loading\n- animation performance\n\nAvoid:\n- huge autoplay videos on mobile\n- unnecessary JavaScript\n- animation on every DOM element\n- excessive blur\n- excessive canvas effects\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n26. MOTION SYSTEM\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nUse a consistent motion language.\n\nEntrance:\n\nopacity 0 \342\206\222 1\ny 40 \342\206\222 0\n\nImage reveal:\n\nclip-path inset \342\206\222 full image\n\nImage hover:\n\nscale 1 \342\206\222 1.04\n\nScroll image:\n\nscale 1.08 \342\206\222 1\n\nParallax:\n\nforeground = small movement\nbackground = slower movement\n\nText:\n\nstaggered character/line reveal\n\nPinned sections:\n\nslow cinematic transitions\n\nAll animation should feel deliberate.\n\nThink:\n\n\"luxury editorial motion\"\n\nnot:\n\n\"motion graphics demo.\"\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n27. DECORATIVE LANGUAGE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate reusable decorative elements inspired by the real caf\303\251:\n\n- aqua arch frames\n- floral borders\n- small gold lines\n- botanical illustrations\n- subtle paper texture\n- ornamental corner details\n- curved shapes\n- thin architectural outlines\n\nUse them sparingly.\n\nDo not turn every section into decoration.\n\nThe photographs should remain the hero.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n28. DESIGN QUALITY BAR\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe final website should feel closer to:\n\nAwwwards-quality restaurant experience\n+\npremium editorial magazine\n+\nromantic European garden caf\303\251\n+\nmodern Indian caf\303\251 website\n\nIt should NOT feel like:\n\nrestaurant template\nWordPress theme\nSaaS landing page\ngeneric AI-generated website\nDribbble concept that cannot actually be used\n\nEvery interaction must have a purpose.\n\nEvery animation must support the story.\n\nEvery section must contribute to either:\n\nDESIRE\nTRUST\nDISCOVERY\nEXPERIENCE\nCONVERSION\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n29. CONTENT ACCURACY\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThis is extremely important.\n\nNever fabricate:\n\n- menu items\n- prices\n- ingredients\n- reviews\n- awards\n- chef names\n- restaurant history\n- opening hours\n- address\n- phone numbers\n- social media statistics\n- reservation availability\n- facilities\n- events\n\nUse only information provided by the client or verified source material.\n\nWhere information is missing, create a clearly marked placeholder or omit the claim.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n30. FINAL EXPERIENCE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe visitor journey should feel like:\n\nGoogle search\n\342\206\223\nBeautiful entrance\n\342\206\223\n\"This place looks amazing.\"\n\342\206\223\nDiscover caf\303\251 atmosphere\n\342\206\223\nSee real food\n\342\206\223\nExplore menu\n\342\206\223\nSee flowers/interior\n\342\206\223\nImagine visiting\n\342\206\223\nOrder on Swiggy / Call / Directions / Reserve\n\342\206\223\nVisit Blueberrys Caf\303\251\n\nThe website should sell the EXPERIENCE of Blueberrys Caf\303\251, not merely list its menu.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n31. IMPLEMENTATION PRINCIPLE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nDo not build every section independently.\n\nCreate a coherent design system first.\n\nCreate reusable components:\n\nNavbar\nHero\nArchFrame\nFloralDecoration\nRevealImage\nParallaxImage\nFoodCard\nMenuCategory\nMenuOverlay\nEditorialGallery\nExperienceSection\nLocationSection\nOrderCTA\nFooter\n\nCreate reusable animation utilities.\n\nKeep the code clean and production-ready.\n\nUse semantic HTML.\n\nEnsure accessibility.\n\nEnsure keyboard navigation.\n\nEnsure mobile responsiveness.\n\nEnsure animations can be disabled through prefers-reduced-motion.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n32. FINAL CREATIVE DIRECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe final website should make someone who has never visited Blueberrys Caf\303\251 think:\n\n\"I want to go there.\"\n\nIt should make someone who has already visited think:\n\n\"Yes. This feels exactly like Blueberrys.\"\n\nDo not chase visual complexity for its own sake.\n\nBuild an unforgettable digital representation of the real caf\303\251.\n\nThe website should feel like opening a beautiful floral caf\303\251 storybook and slowly walking through it.\n\nBUILD THE COMPLETE EXPERIENCE."
    items {
      text: "# MASTER IMPLEMENTATION PROMPT\n# BLUEBERRYS CAF\303\211 \342\200\224 CINEMATIC FLORAL RESTAURANT WEBSITE\n\nYou are an elite frontend engineer, creative web designer, interaction designer and motion designer specializing in premium restaurant and hospitality websites.\n\nYour task is to design and build a highly polished, immersive, animated website for:\n\nBLUEBERRYS CAF\303\211\n\nThis is NOT a generic restaurant template.\n\nThe website must feel like a digital extension of the actual Blueberrys Caf\303\251 shown in the provided reference photographs.\n\nThe physical caf\303\251 has a distinctive visual identity:\n- aqua / turquoise architectural details\n- soft cream walls\n- abundant pink flowers\n- floral garden murals\n- decorative arches\n- European/fairytale garden atmosphere\n- elegant chandeliers\n- teal and blue furniture\n- romantic, playful and photogenic interiors\n- warm ambient lighting\n- decorative ornamental details\n- caf\303\251 / casual dining atmosphere\n\nThe website should make a visitor feel:\n\n\"Entering Blueberrys Caf\303\251.\"\n\nThe experience should feel premium, warm, romantic, playful and cinematic rather than corporate or overly minimal.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n1. CORE DESIGN DIRECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nDesign language:\n\nFLORAL EUROPEAN GARDEN \303\227 ROMANTIC CAF\303\211 \303\227 EDITORIAL FOOD PHOTOGRAPHY \303\227 CINEMATIC WEB MOTION\n\nDo NOT use the typical:\n- generic restaurant template\n- black luxury restaurant aesthetic\n- generic beige food website\n- excessive glassmorphism\n- corporate SaaS cards\n- excessive rounded rectangles\n- generic stock photography\n\nInstead use:\n- large editorial photography\n- organic shapes\n- architectural arches\n- floral framing\n- asymmetric layouts\n- oversized typography\n- layered imagery\n- subtle textures\n- decorative borders\n- soft shadows\n- elegant serif typography\n- refined sans-serif supporting typography\n- carefully controlled motion\n- generous whitespace\n\nThe design should feel handcrafted and visually connected to the physical caf\303\251.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n2. COLOR SYSTEM\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBuild the visual system around the actual caf\303\251.\n\nPrimary colors:\n\nAqua / Caf\303\251 Blue:\n#75C9D0\n\nDeep Teal:\n#155E68\n\nSoft Cream:\n#F8F1E5\n\nWarm Ivory:\n#FFF9EF\n\nBlossom Pink:\n#E98FA7\n\nDeep Blossom:\n#C94F72\n\nMuted Rose:\n#D97891\n\nGarden Green:\n#557B58\n\nSoft Gold:\n#D6B46A\n\nText:\n#24383A\n\nUse the colors with restraint.\n\nCream and ivory should dominate large surfaces.\n\nAqua and teal should define architectural/navigation elements.\n\nPink should appear as a visual accent inspired by the real flowers.\n\nGold should be used sparingly for premium details.\n\nDo not make the website overly colorful.\n\nThe goal is sophisticated floral elegance, not childish candy colors.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n3. TYPOGRAPHY\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nUse a sophisticated editorial typography combination.\n\nSuggested:\n\nDisplay / headlines:\nPlayfair Display\nor Cormorant Garamond\n\nBody:\nInter\nor Manrope\n\nNavigation:\nclean modern sans-serif\n\nUse large editorial headlines with generous line height.\n\nExamples:\n\n\"Where Every Moment Blooms.\"\n\n\"Come for the Coffee.\nStay for the Moment.\"\n\n\"A Little Garden.\nA Lot of Flavor.\"\n\nDo not fill the website with marketing slogans.\n\nUse typography as part of the visual composition.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n4. GLOBAL EXPERIENCE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe website should behave like an immersive visual story.\n\nImplement:\n\n- smooth scrolling using Lenis\n- GSAP ScrollTrigger for major scroll animations\n- subtle parallax\n- image reveal animations\n- masked image reveals\n- slow scale animations\n- text stagger animations\n- horizontal scrolling where appropriate\n- hover image transformations\n- organic morphing shapes\n- pinned sections\n- subtle floating floral elements\n- elegant page transitions\n\nAnimations must feel expensive.\n\nUse:\n- 0.6s\342\200\2231.5s reveals\n- slow easing\n- power3.out / power4.out\n- gentle scale\n- opacity\n- clip-path\n- transform\n- staggered text\n\nAvoid:\n- aggressive bouncing\n- excessive spinning\n- fast transitions\n- random animations everywhere\n- animation that makes the site difficult to navigate\n\nMotion should support storytelling.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n5. NAVIGATION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a premium sticky navigation.\n\nDesktop:\n\nLeft:\nBlueberrys Caf\303\251 logo\n\nCenter:\nHome\nOur Caf\303\251\nMenu\nGallery\nExperience\n\nRight:\n\"Order Online\"\n\"Reserve / Contact\"\n\nThe navigation should initially blend naturally with the hero.\n\nWhen scrolling:\n- transition into a cream/aqua navigation surface\n- add subtle shadow\n- slightly reduce height\n- animate the logo smoothly\n\nMobile:\nUse a beautiful full-screen menu.\n\nThe mobile menu should feel like opening a caf\303\251 journal or floral postcard rather than a generic hamburger drawer.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n6. HERO \342\200\224 \"ENTER BLUEBERRYS\"\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe hero is the most important section.\n\nUse the REAL caf\303\251 photographs supplied by the user.\n\nDo not replace them with AI-generated restaurant imagery.\n\nCreate a cinematic layered hero.\n\nPossible composition:\n\nFULL SCREEN HERO\n\nBackground:\nLarge photograph of the Blueberrys interior.\n\nLayer 1:\nsubtle floral texture / grain\n\nLayer 2:\nlarge architectural arch shape\n\nLayer 3:\nfloating floral image\n\nLayer 4:\nheadline\n\nLayer 5:\nsmall caf\303\251 details\n\nHeadline:\n\n\"Where Every Moment Blooms.\"\n\nSupporting text:\n\n\"Good food, beautiful spaces and little moments worth remembering.\"\n\nCTA:\n\n\"Explore the Caf\303\251\"\n\nSecondary CTA:\n\n\"View Menu\"\n\nAnimation:\n\nAt page load:\n- background image slowly scales from 1.08 \342\206\222 1\n- headline reveals line by line\n- floral elements drift slightly\n- logo fades upward\n- CTA appears after headline\n\nAs the user scrolls:\n- hero image slowly zooms\n- foreground floral elements move at different speeds\n- architectural arch expands\n- headline moves upward\n- next section visually emerges through the arch\n\nCreate the feeling that the visitor is physically moving into the caf\303\251.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n7. SIGNATURE INTRODUCTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nAfter the hero, create a calm editorial section.\n\nLarge typography:\n\n\"More than a caf\303\251.\"\n\nThen:\n\n\"A place for coffee, conversations, celebrations,\nquick bites, long lunches and photographs you\'ll\nwant to keep.\"\n\nUse a large photograph on one side.\n\nUse subtle parallax.\n\nDo not use a standard two-column card.\n\nThe photograph should partially overlap the section boundary.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n8. THE BLUEBERRYS WORLD\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate an immersive visual section introducing the caf\303\251 atmosphere.\n\nUse the actual interior photographs.\n\nCreate an asymmetric editorial layout:\n\n- large caf\303\251 interior image\n- small detail photograph\n- floral photograph\n- architectural arch photograph\n\nPossible labels:\n\nTHE SPACE\nTHE FLOWERS\nTHE DETAILS\nTHE MOMENTS\n\nImages should move at slightly different speeds during scrolling.\n\nUse subtle reveal masks.\n\nSome images can overlap.\n\nThe layout should resemble a high-end editorial magazine spread.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n9. SIGNATURE FOOD SECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate:\n\n\"Something Delicious Is Waiting.\"\n\nShow selected menu items using the actual menu information visible in the provided menu photographs.\n\nImportant:\n\nDo not invent dishes.\n\nDo not invent prices.\n\nDo not invent ingredients.\n\nUse only clearly readable menu information supplied by the user.\n\nOrganize the menu into visual categories such as:\n\nPASTA\nPIZZA\nSANDWICHES\nCOFFEE\nTEA\nICED DRINKS\nMOJITOS\nSHAKES\nJUICES\nSOUPS\n\nDisplay food photography where available.\n\nCards should NOT look like standard ecommerce cards.\n\nInstead:\n\nlarge food image\nsmall category label\ndish name\nshort description\nprice\nsubtle hover interaction\n\nOn hover:\n- image zooms slightly\n- card shifts a few pixels\n- typography transitions\n- decorative accent appears\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n10. MENU EXPERIENCE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a dedicated interactive menu experience.\n\nDesktop:\n\nClicking:\n\n\"Explore Full Menu\"\n\nopens a full-screen menu overlay.\n\nThe overlay should feel like opening a beautifully designed physical caf\303\251 menu.\n\nUse:\n- cream paper-like background\n- aqua borders\n- pink decorative floral elements\n- elegant typography\n- category navigation\n- dish names\n- descriptions\n- vegetarian/chicken indicators where applicable\n- prices\n\nUse subtle scroll animation inside the menu.\n\nDo NOT use a boring table.\n\nUse editorial menu typography.\n\nExample:\n\nPASTA\n\nALFREDO PASTA ........ \342\202\271389 / \342\202\271419\n\nCREAMY CHEESE & GARLIC PASTA\n\342\202\271369 / \342\202\271399\n\n...\n\nFor all menu data, preserve the source exactly.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n11. FOOD DISCOVERY INTERACTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a visually interesting food interaction.\n\nWhen the user moves between categories:\n\nPizza \342\206\222 Pasta \342\206\222 Sandwiches \342\206\222 Coffee \342\206\222 Drinks\n\nthe large visual image should change.\n\nUse:\n- crossfade\n- scale\n- clip-path reveal\n- slight horizontal movement\n\nAvoid hard page reloads.\n\nThe experience should feel like browsing a physical menu.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n12. CAF\303\211 EXPERIENCE SECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a large pinned cinematic section.\n\nHeadline:\n\n\"Come for the food.\nStay for the atmosphere.\"\n\nUse a full-screen photograph of the actual caf\303\251.\n\nAs the visitor scrolls:\n\nStage 1:\nlarge interior photograph\n\nStage 2:\nimage slowly zooms\n\nStage 3:\ntext appears\n\nStage 4:\nsmall detail images appear around it\n\nStage 5:\ntransition into floral imagery\n\nThis should be one of the site\'s signature animation moments.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n13. FLORAL GARDEN SECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe pink floral d\303\251cor is one of the strongest characteristics of this caf\303\251.\n\nMake it a major part of the website.\n\nCreate a section titled:\n\n\"Step Into the Garden.\"\n\nUse the floral wall and pink tree photographs.\n\nDesign:\n\nlarge vertical photograph\noverlapping floral close-up\nsmall decorative typography\nsoft aqua arch\n\nAs the user scrolls:\n- flowers slowly move at different depths\n- image reveals through an arch\n- text fades in\n- background gently shifts\n\nUse restrained motion.\n\nDo NOT make flowers fly around the screen.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n14. PHOTO MOMENTS / INSTAGRAM-STYLE GALLERY\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a premium editorial gallery.\n\nUse actual restaurant photographs.\n\nDo NOT make a uniform 3\303\2273 grid.\n\nUse an asymmetric masonry/editorial layout.\n\nMix:\n\nportrait\nlandscape\nsquare\nclose-up\nwide interior\nfood\nflowers\narchitectural details\ncustomer moments\n\nImages should have different sizes.\n\nUse scroll-driven parallax.\n\nOn hover:\n- image slightly zooms\n- overlay appears\n- subtle caption appears\n\nPossible labels:\n\nCAF\303\211\nFOOD\nFLOWERS\nMOMENTS\nDETAILS\n\nClicking an image opens a full-screen lightbox.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n15. \"A PLACE FOR EVERY MOMENT\"\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a visual section showing the types of experiences the caf\303\251 supports.\n\nBased on the provided information, the website can present:\n\nDINE IN\nTAKEAWAY\nDELIVERY\nCOFFEE & QUICK BITES\nDESSERTS\nGROUP MOMENTS\n\nDo not make unsupported claims about services.\n\nOnly display services confirmed by the restaurant\'s actual information.\n\nEach item should have an image and a subtle interaction.\n\nUse large typography rather than conventional cards.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n16. SPECIAL MOMENTS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a section for:\n\nBirthdays\nDates\nFriends\nFamily\nCasual coffee\nCelebrations\nSolo caf\303\251 time\n\nDo not claim the restaurant officially provides private events unless confirmed.\n\nFrame this as:\n\n\"Moments that feel better here.\"\n\nUse the real customer/interior photographs where appropriate.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n17. TESTIMONIAL / SOCIAL PROOF\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate an elegant testimonial section.\n\nUse real customer reviews only if review text is supplied.\n\nDo NOT fabricate reviews.\n\nIf no verified reviews are available:\n\nInstead create:\n\n\"Your Blueberrys Moment\"\n\nwith a CTA:\n\n\"Share your experience.\"\n\nThe section can visually reference social media without inventing follower counts.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n18. LOCATION / VISIT SECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate:\n\n\"Come Find Us.\"\n\nInclude:\n\n- address\n- Google Maps location\n- phone number\n- opening hours\n\nOnly use verified information supplied by the client.\n\nAdd:\n\n\"Get Directions\"\n\n\"Call Caf\303\251\"\n\n\"Order Online\"\n\n\"Reserve\"\n\nFor online ordering, link to the restaurant\'s actual Swiggy page when supplied.\n\nDo NOT create a fake ordering system.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n19. SWIGGY / ORDER ONLINE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe restaurant already sells online through Swiggy.\n\nMake this an important conversion point.\n\nCreate a beautiful section:\n\n\"Craving Blueberrys?\"\n\n\"Enjoy your favourites wherever you are.\"\n\nCTA:\n\n\"Order on Swiggy\"\n\nThe button must link to the restaurant\'s actual Swiggy listing.\n\nDo not build an unnecessary custom ecommerce checkout.\n\nThe website\'s job is discovery + trust + experience + conversion.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n20. RESERVATION / CONTACT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIf reservation functionality is available:\n\nCreate a refined reservation/contact section.\n\nFields:\n\nName\nPhone\nDate\nTime\nGuests\nMessage\n\nIf there is no actual reservation backend:\n\nDo NOT create a fake booking confirmation.\n\nInstead use:\n\n\"Reserve / Enquire\"\n\nand connect to the appropriate phone, WhatsApp or booking system supplied by the client.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n21. FOOTER\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a beautiful oversized footer.\n\nCream background.\n\nLarge text:\n\n\"See you at Blueberrys.\"\n\nUse a large floral image partially extending into the footer.\n\nInclude:\n\nBlueberrys Caf\303\251\nAddress\nPhone\nOpening Hours\nInstagram\nSwiggy\nGoogle Maps\n\nNavigation links.\n\nCopyright.\n\nThe footer should feel like the final page of a beautiful travel journal.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n22. SIGNATURE TRANSITION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBefore the footer, create one final cinematic transition.\n\nLarge image of the caf\303\251.\n\nText:\n\n\"Until the next cup.\"\n\nThen slowly fade into:\n\nBLUEBERRYS CAF\303\211\n\nThe flower imagery should remain subtly visible.\n\nThis should be the emotional ending of the website.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n23. IMAGE HANDLING\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nThe supplied photographs are the source of truth for the visual identity.\n\nUse the provided Blueberrys Caf\303\251 photographs wherever appropriate.\n\nPrioritize:\n\n1. real caf\303\251 interior\n2. real floral d\303\251cor\n3. real architecture\n4. real menu photographs\n5. real food photographs\n6. real customer atmosphere\n\nDo not replace them with generic restaurant stock images.\n\nDo not use random Unsplash photographs simply to fill sections.\n\nIf a required visual asset is missing:\n\nUse an elegant placeholder structure rather than inventing an unrelated image.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n24. RESPONSIVE DESIGN\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nDesktop:\nimmersive full-screen layouts\nasymmetric compositions\nlarge typography\nrich parallax\n\nTablet:\nreduce overlapping elements\nmaintain editorial composition\n\nMobile:\nDO NOT simply shrink desktop.\n\nCreate a dedicated mobile composition.\n\nPriorities:\n\n- fast loading\n- readable menu\n- easy Swiggy ordering\n- easy calling\n- easy navigation\n- beautiful food imagery\n- smooth but restrained animation\n\nOn mobile, reduce:\n- heavy parallax\n- complex pinned animations\n- excessive floating elements\n\nRespect prefers-reduced-motion.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n25. PERFORMANCE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThis is a real restaurant website.\n\nIt must be beautiful AND fast.\n\nUse:\n\nNext.js\nTypeScript\nTailwind CSS\nGSAP / ScrollTrigger\nLenis where appropriate\nFramer Motion only where useful\n\nOptimize:\n- image sizes\n- lazy loading\n- responsive images\n- WebP / AVIF\n- video loading\n- animation performance\n\nAvoid:\n- huge autoplay videos on mobile\n- unnecessary JavaScript\n- animation on every DOM element\n- excessive blur\n- excessive canvas effects\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n26. MOTION SYSTEM\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nUse a consistent motion language.\n\nEntrance:\n\nopacity 0 \342\206\222 1\ny 40 \342\206\222 0\n\nImage reveal:\n\nclip-path inset \342\206\222 full image\n\nImage hover:\n\nscale 1 \342\206\222 1.04\n\nScroll image:\n\nscale 1.08 \342\206\222 1\n\nParallax:\n\nforeground = small movement\nbackground = slower movement\n\nText:\n\nstaggered character/line reveal\n\nPinned sections:\n\nslow cinematic transitions\n\nAll animation should feel deliberate.\n\nThink:\n\n\"luxury editorial motion\"\n\nnot:\n\n\"motion graphics demo.\"\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n27. DECORATIVE LANGUAGE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate reusable decorative elements inspired by the real caf\303\251:\n\n- aqua arch frames\n- floral borders\n- small gold lines\n- botanical illustrations\n- subtle paper texture\n- ornamental corner details\n- curved shapes\n- thin architectural outlines\n\nUse them sparingly.\n\nDo not turn every section into decoration.\n\nThe photographs should remain the hero.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n28. DESIGN QUALITY BAR\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe final website should feel closer to:\n\nAwwwards-quality restaurant experience\n+\npremium editorial magazine\n+\nromantic European garden caf\303\251\n+\nmodern Indian caf\303\251 website\n\nIt should NOT feel like:\n\nrestaurant template\nWordPress theme\nSaaS landing page\ngeneric AI-generated website\nDribbble concept that cannot actually be used\n\nEvery interaction must have a purpose.\n\nEvery animation must support the story.\n\nEvery section must contribute to either:\n\nDESIRE\nTRUST\nDISCOVERY\nEXPERIENCE\nCONVERSION\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n29. CONTENT ACCURACY\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThis is extremely important.\n\nNever fabricate:\n\n- menu items\n- prices\n- ingredients\n- reviews\n- awards\n- chef names\n- restaurant history\n- opening hours\n- address\n- phone numbers\n- social media statistics\n- reservation availability\n- facilities\n- events\n\nUse only information provided by the client or verified source material.\n\nWhere information is missing, create a clearly marked placeholder or omit the claim.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n30. FINAL EXPERIENCE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe visitor journey should feel like:\n\nGoogle search\n\342\206\223\nBeautiful entrance\n\342\206\223\n\"This place looks amazing.\"\n\342\206\223\nDiscover caf\303\251 atmosphere\n\342\206\223\nSee real food\n\342\206\223\nExplore menu\n\342\206\223\nSee flowers/interior\n\342\206\223\nImagine visiting\n\342\206\223\nOrder on Swiggy / Call / Directions / Reserve\n\342\206\223\nVisit Blueberrys Caf\303\251\n\nThe website should sell the EXPERIENCE of Blueberrys Caf\303\251, not merely list its menu.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n31. IMPLEMENTATION PRINCIPLE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nDo not build every section independently.\n\nCreate a coherent design system first.\n\nCreate reusable components:\n\nNavbar\nHero\nArchFrame\nFloralDecoration\nRevealImage\nParallaxImage\nFoodCard\nMenuCategory\nMenuOverlay\nEditorialGallery\nExperienceSection\nLocationSection\nOrderCTA\nFooter\n\nCreate reusable animation utilities.\n\nKeep the code clean and production-ready.\n\nUse semantic HTML.\n\nEnsure accessibility.\n\nEnsure keyboard navigation.\n\nEnsure mobile responsiveness.\n\nEnsure animations can be disabled through prefers-reduced-motion.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n32. FINAL CREATIVE DIRECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe final website should make someone who has never visited Blueberrys Caf\303\251 think:\n\n\"I want to go there.\"\n\nIt should make someone who has already visited think:\n\n\"Yes. This feels exactly like Blueberrys.\"\n\nDo not chase visual complexity for its own sake.\n\nBuild an unforgettable digital representation of the real caf\303\251.\n\nThe website should feel like opening a beautiful floral caf\303\251 storybook and slowly walking through it.\n\nBUILD THE COMPLETE EXPERIENCE."
    }
  }
}
