  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the immersive, cinematic restaurant experience for Blueberrys Caf\303\251. The design and motion strictly follow your creative direction, prioritizing elegant editorial composition and refined aesthetic storytelling.\n\n### Visual & Interactive Design\n*   **The Caf\303\251 Identity**: Engineered a custom theme utilizing the requested palette\342\200\224incorporating Cafe Aqua, Deep Teal, Soft Cream, Blossom Pink, and Warm Ivory across the layout. \n*   **Typographic Pairing**: Integrated sophisticated typography using *Playfair Display* for sweeping, oversized editorial headlines and *Manrope* for clean, modern body copy.\n*   **Cinematic Web Motion**: Implemented smooth momentum scrolling using Lenis alongside GSAP-style ScrollTrigger animations via Framer Motion. This includes carefully timed slow scales on background imagery, staggered text reveals, layered parallax, and image clipping masks throughout the narrative.\n*   **Elegant Placeholders**: Since the real photography will be supplied later, I engineered a `PlaceholderImage` system that renders elegant, minimal cream-and-teal architectural boxes. This ensures the editorial layout remains balanced and beautiful while waiting for your actual image assets, strictly avoiding generic AI or Unsplash substitutions as requested.\n\n### Narrative Architecture\n*   **Hero & Introduction**: A layered, full-screen opening statement featuring staggered text reveals and an architectural floating arch to immediately pull the visitor into the atmosphere.\n*   **The Blueberrys World**: A rich, asymmetric masonry section mimicking a high-end magazine spread, bringing together details, flowers, and spatial photography at different scroll depths.\n*   **Interactive Menu Discovery**: Created an interactive menu discovery section where navigating categories seamlessly transitions the central hero imagery. Accessing the full menu opens a bespoke full-screen overlay reminiscent of a physical caf\303\251 menu printed on cream paper.\n*   **Pinned Atmosphere**: A signature, three-stage cinematic pinned scroll moment showcasing the transition from atmosphere to intimate detail.\n*   **Actionable Footer & Utility**: Constructed practical conversion points including Swiggy integration and a beautifully oversized, journal-style footer. \n\nThe application is thoroughly responsive, focusing on a tactile experience across all devices. Please let me know if you would like any adjustments to the motion timings or layout compositions!"
    thinking: "**Reviewing the Application**\n\nI\'ve finished building the application, and it\'s fully functional! Now, I\'m reviewing the implementation. I used strict Tailwind CSS and created components for each section using Framer Motion (imported from `motion/react`). I also implemented smooth scrolling using `lenis/react`, and incorporated elegant typography with Playfair Display and Manrope fonts.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed the immersive, cinematic restaurant experience for Blueberrys Caf\303\251. The design and motion strictly follow your creative direction, prioritizing elegant editorial composition and refined aesthetic storytelling.\n\n### Visual & Interactive Design\n*   **The Caf\303\251 Identity**: Engineered a custom theme utilizing the requested palette\342\200\224incorporating Cafe Aqua, Deep Teal, Soft Cream, Blossom Pink, and Warm Ivory across the layout. \n*   **Typographic Pairing**: Integrated sophisticated typography using *Playfair Display* for sweeping, oversized editorial headlines and *Manrope* for clean, modern body copy.\n*   **Cinematic Web Motion**: Implemented smooth momentum scrolling using Lenis alongside GSAP-style ScrollTrigger animations via Framer Motion. This includes carefully timed slow scales on background imagery, staggered text reveals, layered parallax, and image clipping masks throughout the narrative.\n*   **Elegant Placeholders**: Since the real photography will be supplied later, I engineered a `PlaceholderImage` system that renders elegant, minimal cream-and-teal architectural boxes. This ensures the editorial layout remains balanced and beautiful while waiting for your actual image assets, strictly avoiding generic AI or Unsplash substitutions as requested.\n\n### Narrative Architecture\n*   **Hero & Introduction**: A layered, full-screen opening statement featuring staggered text reveals and an architectural floating arch to immediately pull the visitor into the atmosphere.\n*   **The Blueberrys World**: A rich, asymmetric masonry section mimicking a high-end magazine spread, bringing together details, flowers, and spatial photography at different scroll depths.\n*   **Interactive Menu Discovery**: Created an interactive menu discovery section where navigating categories seamlessly transitions the central hero imagery. Accessing the full menu opens a bespoke full-screen overlay reminiscent of a physical caf\303\251 menu printed on cream paper.\n*   **Pinned Atmosphere**: A signature, three-stage cinematic pinned scroll moment showcasing the transition from atmosphere to intimate detail.\n*   **Actionable Footer & Utility**: Constructed practical conversion points including Swiggy integration and a beautifully oversized, journal-style footer. \n\nThe application is thoroughly responsive, focusing on a tactile experience across all devices. Please let me know if you would like any adjustments to the motion timings or layout compositions!"
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 73479471
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
