    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHRxDvYZEN_vE9U0SjWovluBao9QJe8f5pNaUv3SO9xujnE-8YevvMQSQsnxsJwJH6ybKLp3Ylrbg3pfl3XQ7EQhclLgP-tCfb1WlY8EMzAa1f6mhjTo03daE8FnScFgRYgo7CEvRBwZPBPw6s8"
      title: "github.com"
    }
    summary: "The GitHub repository \"github.com/MengTo/kage\" hosts a project called \"Kage,\" which is described as an interactive, five-chapter night walk through a Kyoto mountain temple. The experience is rendered live using Three.js[1][2][3][4][5].\n\n\"Kage\" is an independent design study inspired by Japanese temple architecture and night gardens. It functions as a small static site, where the `index.html` file contains the document structure, CSS, procedural scene construction, scroll choreography, and interaction logic. It leverages a vendored Three.js r149 build for WebGL rendering without the need for a package manager or build step[1].\n\nKey features of the \"Kage\" experience include:\n*   Moving a live WebGL camera through a mountain temple as the page scrolls[1].\n*   Combining procedural elements like architecture, lantern light, fog, rain, drifting leaves, and a vermilion moon[1].\n*   Layering editorial typography, generated cinematic scene plates, and alpha-preserving WebP foreground elements over the 3D world[1][6].\n*   Implementing section-specific fade and blur transitions, chapter navigation, a responsive mobile layout, reduced-motion behavior, and a custom cursor for precise pointer devices[1].\n\nThe project\'s design and attribution notes indicate that the cinematic scene plates and foreground artwork were generated using GPT Image 2, then art-directed and composed with the live Three.js scene[1]. The aim was to create a cinematic WebGL experience that feels like an editorial art book moving through a live 3D world, rather than a conventional product landing page[6].\n\nSources:\n[1] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH5_kNaBOIjXuq_X9h-tiMBwMIUl5YUSd12wLONnQnSKpSmMVK5MGGhSwgeNJh1ScQw31KVX4d1aFe2eF7nRsNFR1EQqJkcQ_p4fuDkchFtPovkVS0jeirqIw==)\n[2] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF4Jr-qNTIJWMqE3w7_dSiRlsgOuBJ3FjgDyNf-_tRL5sePDHw46ncl5X_I6qypt2v9mv2tJ-2cRCB5gxf2xQb3OvWidvEhEc767_dLmWSQZrtEGYT5gT-WWuh-er4aoRui)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHrB6ln6vehkgABqCN9JNL277vpGkLAfDmB-iz8oBu9OoQeyaTy3IT5a038SQHtin6WFMoM8G9Q25ugxD52xRlue146EGdYAX7UTQ4DfAdGCpHlMXLCCoUvS4KhwQR_MQ==)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEmsF3mienlLowh3jiewyFk9jpILbJLWrSYlwP6Ij4QLYi-BzC46NqcJ6k9FCMM1thjuAhlSar_hLG2jjV6idBbWnYnT5Qmd2lcpUekp_-2ztxSVEyhQ-Fr0Voj2wsQ_MWE2g==)\n[5] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHLbI2j8lKLfrasIKKwoxtwHhUOYeeM5-M271ZGBgRyergNzykqWe0yA9ZUsPuyBD30QEa6tKzeWc9fQRsb_2JJtQK_jq-4DP0ZCpHJQGGkSP3JP1Q2vwV_cMenELEcH-5CANxlrEc5ctrIrMVc)\n[6] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHRxDvYZEN_vE9U0SjWovluBao9QJe8f5pNaUv3SO9xujnE-8YevvMQSQsnxsJwJH6ybKLp3Ylrbg3pfl3XQ7EQhclLgP-tCfb1WlY8EMzAa1f6mhjTo03daE8FnScFgRYgo7CEvRBwZPBPw6s8)"
