  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Exploring Visual Narratives**\n\nI\'m currently captivated by MengTo\'s \"Kage,\" specifically how it blends WebGL (Three.js) with editorial design. The interactive, cinematic scroll experience, the layering of typography and images over a dynamic 3D world is fascinating. It is a very immersive experience, and a great use case of this new generation of design tools.\n\n\n**Adapting Design Concepts**\n\nI\'m now focusing on adapting Kage\'s design for Blueberrys Caf\303\251. The existing React/Tailwind/Framer Motion stack necessitates a careful approach. I\'m considering using `react-three-fiber` or layered 2.5D Framer Motion for the background to simulate the atmosphere. Specifics, such as floral dust and drifting petals, are key. I must consider performance implications with Three.js, so I need to decide between it or a lighter `framer-motion` implementation.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specifics for the Blueberrys Caf\303\251 project. I\'m leaning toward a 2.5D parallax scroll with `framer-motion`, focusing on cinematic layering and custom interactions. Specifically, I\'ll add drifting pink petals/dust as an overlay, and a custom cursor. I want heavy parallax and blur with section-specific fades. We can explore scene plates and overlapping foreground elements. I\'m breaking this down into a custom cursor and atmospheric particle implementation.\n\n\n**Implementing Atmospheric Effects**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating environmental elements. Specifically, I plan to mimic the atmospheric effects of Kage using falling petals and floating dust. My current plan involves wrapping sections in scroll-triggered blur and fade effects. I will implement deep parallax and layering in `Hero.tsx`, `CafeExperience.tsx`, etc., to create a sense of depth. I\'m also considering foreground cutouts. Instead of a night theme, I am leaning into a bright \"immersive layered garden\" vibe. I\'ll stick with standard React/Motion.\n\n\n**Developing Cinematic Interactions**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the practical implementation of my design concepts. I\'m focusing on the technical components, starting with `CustomCursor.tsx` and `AtmosphericParticles.tsx`. I intend to add blur/fade effects using a `CinematicSection.tsx` wrapper for a layered, cinematic feel. I will also be modifying and enhancing `Hero.tsx` and `CafeExperience.tsx` to include parallax and deep zoom.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 14
      nanos: 509780657
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
