  planner_response {
    response: "I have integrated a custom Web Audio API synthesizer engine to provide soft, organic sound effects across the application, enriching the cinematic feel without relying on heavy external audio files.\n\nHere is an overview of the acoustic enhancements:\n\n*   **Audio Synthesis Engine (`audio.ts`)**: Created a lightweight, completely custom synthesizer utilizing the native Web Audio API. It generates sounds procedurally in real-time.\n*   **The Page-Turn Effect**: When utilizing the main navigation links, the page transition overlay is now accompanied by a soft, filtered white-noise sweep. This perfectly simulates the rustling friction of heavy paper turning in a physical journal. \n*   **Ambient Chimes & Interactions**:\n    *   **Hover States**: The custom cursor now tracks hover states to emit a very soft, muted harmonic tick when passing over interactive elements (buttons, links).\n    *   **Menu Engagements**: Opening the full-screen menu overlay triggers a gentle, cinematic bell chord (two sine wave oscillators sweeping through a long decay), whilst closing it triggers the page-turn rustle.\n\nThe audio context safely waits for your first interaction before initializing, ensuring compliance with browser autoplay policies while immediately engaging the senses as you explore the site."
    modified_response: "I have integrated a custom Web Audio API synthesizer engine to provide soft, organic sound effects across the application, enriching the cinematic feel without relying on heavy external audio files.\n\nHere is an overview of the acoustic enhancements:\n\n*   **Audio Synthesis Engine (`audio.ts`)**: Created a lightweight, completely custom synthesizer utilizing the native Web Audio API. It generates sounds procedurally in real-time.\n*   **The Page-Turn Effect**: When utilizing the main navigation links, the page transition overlay is now accompanied by a soft, filtered white-noise sweep. This perfectly simulates the rustling friction of heavy paper turning in a physical journal. \n*   **Ambient Chimes & Interactions**:\n    *   **Hover States**: The custom cursor now tracks hover states to emit a very soft, muted harmonic tick when passing over interactive elements (buttons, links).\n    *   **Menu Engagements**: Opening the full-screen menu overlay triggers a gentle, cinematic bell chord (two sine wave oscillators sweeping through a long decay), whilst closing it triggers the page-turn rustle.\n\nThe audio context safely waits for your first interaction before initializing, ensuring compliance with browser autoplay policies while immediately engaging the senses as you explore the site."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
